/* WHAT COUNTS AS A PRESS of the top or the bottom button is AO_Buttons'
 * answer, not this file's, and it used to be measured here as well: a window
 * of 40 ms to KODE_BUTTON_HOLD_MS between the two edges, under which a press
 * was a glitch and over which it was a hold. Both jobs already have an owner
 * - the 30 ms settle debounce is what a glitch never survives, and a hold is
 * declared by BUTTON_HOLD_SIG, which disarms the press it grew out of - so
 * the window was a second opinion on two settled questions, and it was the
 * worse-informed one: it timed the two DISPATCHES, not the two edges, and
 * only AO_Net sits below this AO. A repaint or a mirror frame
 * between the press and the release stretched the measurement past the hold
 * and a burst that queued both edges compressed it under the floor, and
 * either way the press was dropped without a word. That is the side-button
 * press that went missing after a pad move (2026-09-15).
 */

